SCHEDULE: {"1":"Ann","2":"Finn","3":"Elif","4":"Dev","5":"Ivo","6":"Gus","7":"Cara","8":"Hana","9":"Ben"}
CONFIDENCE: 97

The key deduction: let Finn be in slot f. Elif is f+1 and Dev is f+2. Ivo must come after Elif and not be Dev, so Ivo ≥ f+3. Hana must be at least three slots after Ivo, so Hana ≥ f+6. Ben is right after Hana, so Hana ≤ 8, which forces f = 2. That puts Ann in slot 1, Elif in 3, Dev in 4, Ivo in 5 and Hana in 8, with Ben in 9. Gus must be two slots from Hana, so Gus is 6. The only remaining slot is 7 for Cara. All eleven constraints check out, and this is the only valid arrangement.
